Context: This repo was inherited with no attention to linting or formatting. A full automatic linting pass broke functional code, so formatting and docstring fixes must be done incrementally and safely.

Rule:

For all new or modified code, follow these standards:

Format using Black

Lint using flake8

Ensure top-level docstrings per pydocstyle D100 series (i.e., public modules, classes, methods, and functions must be documented)

Use consistent 4-space indentation

Do not leave functions undocumented

❌ Do NOT run auto-formatters or linters repo-wide because they might break existing code.
🛠️ Fix only what you touch — or what you can clearly see in the local context of the change.

Goal: Gradual convergence toward a clean, stable codebase without compromising working logic.

